Acknowledgement 
 
The success of the whole census operations is attributed to detailed planning and cohesive implementation, 
which could not have been achieved without the support and efforts of many people and organizations.  
I would like to thank the  Minister of Finance, under whose authority the Census was undertaken: the 
Chairperson of the Steering Committee, the CEO and Acting CEO of Finance at the time, and all the members 
for their valuable contributions and suggestions. Former Government Statistician for his leadership, guidance 
and coordination for the success of the census operations. 
My appreciation is extended all agencies under United Nations Tonga, and the Australian Aid for your kind 
donations towards Tonga Census 2021.  I also would like to thank the valuable contribution from the World 
Bank HIES tablets for census data collection.  I would also commend the Statistics for Development Division 
(SDD) of The Pacific Community (SPC), for all the technical assistance they provided.  
My sincere gratitude to the CEO of Education  and other school system – FWC and Sia’atoutai College  for 
allowing some of the teachers and Students to take part in Tonga Census 2021. I also extend sincere thanks to 
every individual who participated Census 2021 as an enumerator and supervisor. I wish to thank the Census 
team of 2021 and all the staffs of the Statistics Department for their valuable contributions throughout the 
Census period.  
Last but not the least, my heartfelt gratefulness to all the people of Tonga for your time, participation and 
honest responses. Your contributions are of vital importance in shaping Tonga’s future and making sure that 
No One is Left Behind. 
For the continuous improvement of statisti cal database for the Kingdom, TSD would welcome constructive 
comments and suggestions from users, planners and policy -makers to indicate areas of interests for future 
report releases. 
 
Faka’apa’apa atu, 
 
……………………………………… 
Sione Lolohea 
Acting Government Statistician 
 
